          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I do this in cold weather?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most stains and sealers specify a minimum of about 50 degrees Fahrenheit for both air and surface, with no frost overnight during the cure. Cold slows the acid reaction and makes water-based products cure poorly. In cool months, work in the warmest part of a dry day, or wait for spring. Rain within a day of staining or sealing can also streak the finish."
          }
        }
