        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Making a concrete patio look like stone is mostly a layout and patience job. Choose the stone you want to imitate, draw a believable pattern, create the joints with a saw or tape, then build color stone by stone with a base and one or two accents. Acid stain gives the most natural mottling; water-based stain is easier and offers more colors.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Finish with careful neutralizing if you used acid, then two thin coats of a decorative concrete sealer. Keep up with a maintenance coat every couple of years and avoid harsh de-icers, and the patio will keep its stone look long after the weekend you spent creating it.
          </p>
